# LOCAL.md

Everything specific to *this* checkout and its owner. Gitignored: it may contain server
addresses, names, employers, document ids and anything else you would not publish. Agents read
it after `AGENTS.md`; rules here override the defaults there. Copy this file to `LOCAL.md` and
fill in what you know; sections you leave empty are fine.

## Instance

- Paperless version, reachable URLs (the token itself stays in `.env`).
- Inbox tag name and id.
- Anything unusual about the configuration (duplicate handling, archive generation, ...).

## Conventions on this instance

- Operating mode if not fully automatic (e.g. "ask before apply").
- Document language and title pattern if different from `<What> (<Who>) - DD.MM.YYYY`.
- Name of the duplicate tag (default `Duplikat-Verdacht`).
- Spelling conventions for correspondents and tags (umlauts vs. ASCII, abbreviations).
- Known inconsistencies that must NOT be cleaned up (two tags meaning the same thing, ...).
- Preferred document types and what they cover.

## About the owner and their documents

- Who the documents belong to (name as it appears on letters), addresses that recur.
- Recurring correspondents and how their documents look (employers, insurers, authorities).
- Known bundle patterns (payroll exports, onboarding packets) and how to split them.
- Open gaps the owner has confirmed (a document that is expected but not in Paperless yet).
- Whether the owner has given standing permission to reuse a signature for filling in their own
  forms with `pipeline/form_fill.py` (default: no - treat any earlier use as one-off unless the
  owner says otherwise), and where the signature file lives on this machine if so.

## Machine-specific setup notes

- Where Tesseract/Ghostscript/poppler live, `TESSDATA_PREFIX`, anything that took a while
  to get working.

## Incident log

One line per run with the date and what was learned. Newest at the bottom.

- YYYY-MM-DD: ...
